The header gives the note number and despatch date (DTM+11). Packages are assigned by their parent CPS id, and release characters are removed: `45?:A` becomes `45:A`, `SEAL??RING-7` becomes `SEAL?RING-7`, and `KL?+20/4` becomes `KL+20/4`. The LIN+9 item follows CPS+10, so it belongs to carton 10.

Structure:
- Pallet 2 (LBL38414879): no loose items. Carton 3 (LBL02844027) holds AX-4471/B; carton 4 (LBL93468265) holds BRKT 45:A.
- Pallet 5 (LBL75286258): loose HUB-9031. Carton 6 (LBL36192323) holds BRKT 45:A and SEAL?RING-7; carton 8 (LBL70483176) holds BRKT 45:A.
- Pallet 9 (LBL60362102): loose BRKT 45:A. Carton 10 (LBL51214392) holds BRKT 45:A and KL+20/4.

Totals sum the same part and unit across all items, for example BRKT 45:A in KGM is 26 + 19 = 45 and in PCE is 65 + 12 + 33 = 110.

